Cared-for days.

Returning after periods of absence.

Meaningful interactions.

Feeding and attention.

Important shared experiences.

These factors also contribute to the creature's eventual awakening eligibility.

5. Creature Life Stages and Awakening

This is the main differentiating feature of CRITTERS.

A creature starts as a pixel-art cat.

Eventually, after developing through its life, it can awaken into its ultimate form: a girl.

The important part is that this is the same creature.

It is not a new NFT, a replacement character or a second identity.

5.1 One soul, two presentations

The cat and awakened girl share:

The same identity.

The same name.

The same personality.

The same DNA.

The same history.

The same attributes.

The same wallet ownership.

The same progression.

The cat remains part of the creature's history and life card.

The awakened girl is simply its next presentation.

5.2 Lily sprite system

The project references an existing Lily sprite pack in the game assets.

The pack includes approximately 70 animation clips, covering expressions and actions such as:

Idle.

Talking.

Waving.

Blushing.

Crying.

Angry reactions.

Eating.

Yawning.

Other expressions and movements.

The plan is to reuse this existing sprite pack.

The girl's appearance is derived from the original cat DNA through a deterministic awakenedLook(dna) function.

The mapping includes:

Cat coat colour → hair colour.

Cat pattern → hair treatment.

Eye genes → eye colour.

Accessories → corresponding visual elements.

Other genes → permitted details of the outfit and presentation.

Rarity can determine which existing presentation variants are available, but should not determine whether a creature can awaken.

The important restriction is that the original DNA is never changed.

No paid skins, holder skins, recolouring or cosmetic modifications to the creature's generated appearance.

5.3 The road from hatch to awakening

Hatch is the start. Awakening is the first morning the life is full enough. Nothing in between is a level bar, a pack, or a fee.

The player does four kinds of things. All four have to have happened. One of them cannot finish the road alone.

Care. Feed her, pet her, talk, play, let her rest. A cared-for day is a day she was fed and the machine was opened. Twelve of those days are required, and they have to fall across at least fourteen calendar days. A single sitting cannot produce them. A weekend cannot produce them. A bigger $SOUL bag makes the meal fill more, so the day is easier to complete. It does not turn two days into twelve.

Trust. It rises from those days, and from coming back after being away. It has to hold, not spike. One afternoon of tapping feed does not max it. Trust has to have stayed high on more than one of the cared-for days.

A journal with different kinds of memory. At least one bond (she was fed, petted, or named), one moment (a scrap, a game, a mess, a scolding), one habit (she slept, or kept a routine), and one away (she noticed a gap, and the owner returned). The away memory is the one a bot cannot finish in an hour.

A fight. At least three scraps, free or paid, or scraps plus a refusal when she was too tired or too hungry to sit. The arena is part of the life. It is not the whole life.

The engine checks this when the machine is opened. The model does not. Money, crystals, rarity, and holdings do not appear in the check.

Neglect pauses the road. If she is starving, or the absence is still open, the count waits. Feeding her and coming back resumes it. The missed days stay written. They are not deleted, and they are not required to be perfect.

Twelve cared-for days across two weeks is the shape. The exact counts can be tuned once people are actually keeping cats. The shape should not change: time, trust, more than one kind of memory, and a few fights.

5.4 The awakening moment

The scene plays the first time the check passes and she is awake on the glass. Not while she is asleep. Not from a button in a shop.

The cat settles. The next frame is the girl, dyed from the coat she already had. Same name. The journal stays open. After that, the same glass plays her clips.

The original cat remains on the life card and in the journal.

