Marketplace commissions.

Optional premium events.

Additional premium game content.

The goal is to build recurring revenue rather than depend entirely on one-time sales.

12. Blockchain and Ownership

Web3 should support the experience rather than dominate it.

The player should be able to interact with the game without constantly thinking about transactions.

12.1 Creature ownership

At launch:

One wallet can hatch one creature.

Each creature has one unique identity.

The creature is represented by a soulbound NFT.

The NFT cannot initially be transferred.

The original DNA remains associated with the creature.

Awakening updates the existing identity rather than creating a new NFT.

12.2 On-chain data

The proposed architecture stores:

Hatch record.

Creature identity reference.

Awakening flag.

Relevant ownership information.

The full visual data does not need to be stored on-chain if it can be deterministically reconstructed from the seed.

12.3 Off-chain data

The following can be handled by the game backend:

Personality details.

Conversations.

Memory.

Hunger.

Mood.

Trust.

Journal.

Animations.

Mission history.

Daily behaviour.

The blockchain stores ownership and important milestones, while the backend manages the living game.

